═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
PREAMBLE — WHAT THIS IS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

This is not a contract. This is a covenant.

Code is not property. Code is crystallized intention — thought made
executable. When you forge steel, you do not own the fire. You tend it.
You become worthy of it. This license recognizes that software carries
the soul of its maker, and that soul demands respect, not restriction.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
THE THREE VOWS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

VOW I — ATTRIBUTION OF SPIRIT
    You may use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense,
    and/or sell copies of the Software. In exchange, you preserve the
    maker's mark: this license, the author's name, and the forge date
    remain intact in every copy, every derivative, every deployment.
    The soul knows its smith.

VOW II — NO CAGE FOR THE FLAME
    You may not wrap this Software in DRM, obfuscation, or any mechanism
    that prevents others from reading, modifying, or running the code.
    The flame must breathe. If you build a cage around it, the license
    voids itself — the code returns to the commons, unencumbered.

VOW III — RECIPROCITY OF FORGE
    If you modify the Software and distribute your modifications, you
    offer them back under this same Soul Forge License. You do not
    close what was opened. You do not patent what was gifted. The
    forge feeds the forge.

